1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,408
In 1861, Harriet Colfax took charge of

2
00:00:03,418 --> 00:00:04,902
Michigan City's lighthouse.

3
00:00:05,132 --> 00:00:07,536
She kept the light burning for 43 years.

4
00:00:07,986 --> 00:00:09,528
She lived in the lighthouse with her

5
00:00:09,538 --> 00:00:11,534
lifelong companion, Ann Hartwell.

6
00:00:11,934 --> 00:00:14,670
In 1871, a pier light was added.

7
00:00:14,900 --> 00:00:17,276
Through 1882, five assistant keepers

8
00:00:17,286 --> 00:00:19,804
served with her: two women and three men.

9
00:00:20,254 --> 00:00:23,864
In 1873, she wrote in her log: A terrible

10
00:00:23,874 --> 00:00:24,786
hurricane tonight.

11
00:00:25,236 --> 00:00:28,456
Until a storm took the pier light in 1886,

12
00:00:28,466 --> 00:00:31,000
she tended it too, even when waves broke

13
00:00:31,010 --> 00:00:32,934
over the walkway and ice coated it.

14
00:00:33,384 --> 00:00:36,515
Harriet retired in 1904, at about 80.

15
00:00:36,745 --> 00:00:38,736
That year, she said she could not bear to

16
00:00:38,746 --> 00:00:40,068
see anyone else light her lamp.

17
00:00:40,298 --> 00:00:41,666
She died the next spring.

18
00:00:42,116 --> 00:00:44,433
Her 1858 lighthouse still stands.

19
00:00:44,663 --> 00:00:46,027
Today, it's a museum.

20
00:00:46,527 --> 00:00:48,570
Comment your town, and it could be next.

